Package: memmon
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: scrollable, man-page-styled Linux memory usage monitor
 memmon reads /proc/meminfo (total/used/free/available memory, buffers,
 cache, shared memory, swap, active/inactive, reclaimable slab,
 dirty/writeback, commit, vmalloc, huge pages, and every other field the
 running kernel exposes) along with the load average, memory pressure
 (PSI), OOM kills and swap activity, zram devices, cgroup v2 memory
 limits and the largest processes, and displays it as a scrollable,
 searchable terminal report with trend sparklines that auto-refreshes on
 a configurable interval. One-shot output is available as text, JSON or
 CSV.
 .
 It also runs headless via a bundled systemd service (enabled and started
 automatically on install, as an unprivileged user), appending
 timestamped snapshots to a daily text, JSON Lines or CSV log, raising
 warning/critical alerts through a configurable hook, and summarising a
 day's log with --report. Old logs are compressed and pruned after a
 configurable retention period (30 days by default; see
 /etc/memmon/memmon.conf).
